  "summary": "A common summer resident. Entirely black, and it may show faint barring below, especially the female. The immature is more blackish brown. The male repeats whoo whoo whee, rising on the last note. The female has a wind-up yow-yow call that rises and dies away. It parasitises boubou shrikes. Months were left unset. The Kemp code VB was left unchanged.",
